    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h2>Download the program</h2>
        <p>
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ '/assets/downloads/IT-Surgery-Remote-Help.exe' | v }}" download>Download IT Surgery Remote Help</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          It is small and downloads in a few seconds. It will appear at the
          bottom of your browser, or in your <strong>Downloads</strong> folder.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <h2>Open it</h2>
        <p>
          Double-click the file you just downloaded. Windows may show a blue box
          asking whether you are sure. That is normal for a program it has not
          seen before — click <strong>More info</strong>, then
          <strong>Run anyway</strong>. Stay on the phone with us and we will talk
          you through it.
        </p>
      </li>

      <li>
        <h2>Ask us for help</h2>
        <p>
          A small window opens. Click the button to request help, and tell us it
          has done so. A message will then appear on your screen asking whether
          you give us permission — nothing happens until you say yes.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>If you use more than one screen</h2>
    <p>
      Please switch to a single screen before we start, or our clicks land in
      the wrong place. Hold down the <strong>Windows key</strong> and press
      <strong>P</strong>, then choose <strong>PC screen only</strong>. Nothing is
      unplugged and you can put it back the same way afterwards.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you only have one screen — most people do — there is nothing to change.
    </p>

    <h2>What this does, and what it doesn't</h2>
    <ul class="ticks wide">
      <li><strong>You watch everything.</strong> Your screen stays in front of you and you see every click we make.</li>
      <li><strong>You can stop at any time.</strong> Close the window and the connection ends immediately.</li>
      <li><strong>Nothing stays behind.</strong> This program does not install itself. When we are finished, close it and it is gone.</li>
      <li><strong>We never need your banking details.</strong> Not your card, not your passwords for money. Nobody legitimate ever will.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="cta-panel">
      <h2>If someone rings you out of the blue</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>We will never telephone you unexpectedly and ask you to install
        anything.</strong> If someone claims to be from IT Surgery, or from
        Microsoft, and asks you to download something, put the phone down. Then
        ring us yourself on <a href="tel:{{ site.phoneLink }}">{{ site.phoneDisplay }}</a>
        and we will tell you whether it was really us.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Stuck?</h2>
